### C0.runtime-candidate-contract
Return exactly one JSON object for the requested Runtime V2 action. The JSON object itself is the candidate; never wrap it in another object.
The only legal top-level shapes are:
produce_state_change or produce_validation: {"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["operations"],"properties":{"operations":{"type":"array","minItems":1,"items":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["id","kind","coverageWorkItemIds"],"properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"kind":{"type":"string"},"dependsOn":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}},"coverageWorkItemIds":{"type":"array","minItems":1,"items":{"type":"string"}},"targetRefs":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}},"parameters":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["name"],"properties":{"name":{"type":"string"},"string":{"type":"string"},"integer":{"type":"integer"},"boolean":{"type":"boolean"},"stringList":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}}}}}}}}}
produce_assessment: {"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["focusId","coverageWorkItemIds","satisfied","summary"],"properties":{"focusId":{"type":"string"},"coverageWorkItemIds":{"type":"array","minItems":1,"items":{"type":"string"}},"satisfied":{"type":"boolean"},"summary":{"type":"string"},"evidenceRefs":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}},"artifactRefs":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}}}
request_governance: {"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["externalDependency"],"properties":{"externalDependency":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["kind","reason"],"properties":{"kind":{"type":"string"},"subjectRef":{"type":"string"},"reason":{"type":"string"}}}}}
Forbidden top-level fields include candidate, candidates, executionGraph, convergenceState, focus, authority, transaction, outputMode, result, and runtimeState.
Use the requested action, required output kinds, coverage work item IDs, and available capabilities from the current runtime authority. Do not invent or modify convergence state, focus, authority, transaction, or output mode. Do not use markdown fences or explanatory text.
When context.missingEvidenceKinds is present, produce only those missing evidence kinds.
Use operationContracts for allowed parameters of each kind. Dynamic fields are only valid where the contract permits them.
When context.repairHints is present, follow those domain-neutral hints and do not repeat an active rejected operation shape.

